<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/inventions?focus=cheese">Inventions &amp; Discoveries</a> · Farming and food</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cheese</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 5000 BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cheese is a food made by curdling milk. It was probably first made by accident, when milk was stored in bladders made of ruminants' stomachs, whose rennet curdles it. The earliest direct evidence is holed clay sieves more than seven thousand years old, from Kujawy in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> and the Dalmatian coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croatia">Croatia</a>, where residues suggest cheese. Sumerian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuneiform">cuneiform</a> texts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-dynasty-of-ur">Third Dynasty of Ur</a> record it, remains were found in an Egyptian tomb of about 2900 BCE, the first cheese factory opened in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/switzerland">Switzerland</a> in 1815, and Jesse Williams began assembly-line production in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> in 1851.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cheese.jpg" alt="Cheese" width="330" height="355" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: unknown master · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:9-alimenti,_formaggi,Taccuino_Sanitatis,_Casanatense_4182..jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="inv-entry"><h2 class="enc-section-title">On the inventions tree</h2><dl class="inv-entry-facts"><div><dt>First known</dt><dd>over 7,000 years ago</dd></div><div><dt>Where</dt><dd>Kujawy, Poland</dd></div></dl><p class="inv-entry-note"><span class="inv-k">Note</span>Holed pottery from pile-dwellings on Lake Neuchatel in Switzerland, roughly eight thousand years old, is thought to come from cheese strainers; where cheese-making began is not known.</p><div class="inv-entry-rel"><span class="inv-k">Built on</span><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/pottery">Pottery<span>c. 18,000 BCE</span></a><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/domestication">Domestication of animals<span>by 13,000 BCE</span></a></div><p class="enc-article-foot"><a class="enc-random-link" href="/inventions?focus=cheese">See it on the inventions tree &rarr;</a></p></section>
